      "stdout": "segment shortcuts.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  time-range                  Update a segment time range or duration.\r\n  move                        Move a segment.\r\n  remove                      Remove a segment.\r\n  split                       Split a segment at given time point(s).\r\n  duplicate                   Duplicate a segment.\r\n  add                         Add a segment to the draft (flat alias of `draft <type> add`).\r\n                              See `draft <type> add --help` for per-type semantics.\r\n\r\nACTION CHAINING\r\n  Shared target:\r\n    lyra-cli draft segment [--ref <draft>] <selector> --action <path> <options> ...\r\n  Per-block targets:\r\n    lyra-cli draft segment [--ref <draft>] --action <path> <selector> <options> ...\r\n  Public selectors:\r\n    --seg-id, --seg-type, --target-track, --seg-index, --time-window\r\n  Rules:\r\n    Put a shared selector before the first --action.\r\n    Without a shared selector, every action block must declare one.\r\n    Do not mix shared and per-block targets in one chain.\r\n    Shortcut paths use space-separated tokens, for example `filter update`.\r\n    Cross-object chains use `draft --action <object> <path> ...` and per-block targets.\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli draft segment <subcommand> --help` for a specific shortcut.\r\n",
